List three real-life scenarios where a multimeter would be used to troubleshoot a computer or smartphone issue, and explain in one line how the multimeter helps in each case.

1.Computer won't power on – Use the multimeter to measure the power supply's output voltages and verify it is delivering the correct power to the motherboard.
2.Smartphone not charging – Use the multimeter to check the charger, USB cable, or battery voltage to identify whether the charging components are functioning properly.
3.Laptop or smartphone has no response after a drop or repair – Use the multimeter's continuity mode to detect broken traces, blown fuses, or damaged connections on the circuit board.
